$ the subject of the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{x-1}{3}\\,⟹\\,x=3{y}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nSo, the parametrization of the curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =(3{t}^{2}+1)\\,i+t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3{t}^{2}+1,\\,y=t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2{y}^{2}\\,i+x\\,j \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}\\,i+(3{t}^{2}+1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}+1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =6t\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2{t}^{2}\\,i+(3{t}^{2}+1)\\,j)\\cdot (6t\\,i+j) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}\\cdot 6t+(3{t}^{2}+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =12{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+1)\\,dt \\\\  & ={[3{t}^{4}+{t}^{3}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3+1+1-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337268 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337269 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337270 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337271 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337272 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1041 "selection" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337272 13194139535202 true] [17592186337267 1110 #uuid "a943557a-c806-5351-947d-3780140e7556" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337268 1034 "8" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337268 1111 #uuid "f4c9b433-6649-5e3f-9efe-73