17592186337287 1089 "q-125238" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535202 true] [17592186337287 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\,i-{e}^{y}\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin traversed counterclockwise from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(0,1).$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337287 1113 #uuid "3b794b22-45f0-563f-b97c-2452d92d75df" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337287 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at the origin. This curve can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & ={e}^{x}\\,i-{e}^{y}\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i-{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})\\,dt \\\\  & ={[{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}-{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi /2}-{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi /2}-({e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}-{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡0}) \\\\  & =1-e-(e-1) \\\\  & =2-2e\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337289 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337290 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337291 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337292 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337293 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1041 "selection" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337292 13194139535202 true] [17592186337288 1110 #uuid "f679b7f0-ecd9-5b84-bbd5-9df73587621c" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337289 1034 "2e" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337289 1111 #uuid "67e04a99-9ba3-5a87-9960-6c84034ffb7d" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337290 1034 "1-e" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337290 1111 #uuid "ec5cc75f-60c1-56ab-8b49-fd0000583386" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337291 1034 "e" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337291 1111 #uuid "197282f6-6e2a-5d7d-9a5d-7d78ec79eddd" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337292 1034 "2-2e" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337292 1111 #uuid "047ea37a-fb73-58e6-a81b-3ab493b3292e" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337293 1034 "0" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337293 1111 #uuid "e2146c88-cbbd-5789-9ee1-9a23d478517c" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337294 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337295 13194139535202 true] [17592186337294 1089 "q-39427" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337294 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535202 true] [17592186337294 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058907/assets/c5e026312ab8a2ccfc61a37246c954b56550316661f158743cc2c46411a97f53.png)\n\nEvaluate ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(y-x)\\,i-x\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=2$  traversed counterclockwise from the point $(\\sqrt{2},0)$ to the point $(0,1).$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337294 1113 #uuid "66073e06-bf27-5b3e-854c-8243f5b08a5b" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337294 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Notice that we can write its equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, our curve is a part-ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $1$ respectively. This curve can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(y-x)\\,i-x\\,j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\sqrt{2}({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-\\sqrt{2}\\,dt \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-\\sqrt{2}t]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}]-[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-0] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}]-[-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337296 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337297 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337298 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337299 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337300 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1041 "selection" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1104 #edb/ref 17592186337300 13194139535202 true] [17592186337295 1110 #uuid "eacd4914-4207-55e6-80e2-b9ed89b1766f" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337296 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337296 1111 #uuid "873039ce-760f-5e07-bf69-f067083634e8" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337297 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337297 1111 #uuid "5f09d875-9ae6-5bab-af23-f750c0f60d26" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337298 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}-\\pi \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337298 1111 #uuid "215d2d10-536d-50ef-afc2-5126679076d5" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337299 1034 "1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337299 1111 #uuid "47c24a06-7f1c-5dc3-bb44-5c2e291e0bfb" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337300 1034 "1-\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{2}" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535202 true] [17592186337300 1111 #uuid "ad82228f-cb5c-58b8-855e-5462618692c7" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337301 1017 #edb/ref 17592186337302 13194139535202 true] [17592186337301 1089 "q-77034" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337301 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535202 true] [17592186337301 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058907/assets/00547d8271d0c277de2bd1992d759e0157a80c9caf05cfb1020550853ae7b8b3.png)\n\nEvaluate the line integral ${\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(x+y)\\,i+(1-x)\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36$  traversed from the point $A(0,3)$ to the point $B(-2,0).$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337301 1113 #uuid "2d10387d-6cca-597b-add1-a27be5676ce8" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337301 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. Notice that we can write its equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nSo, our curve is a part-ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $2$ and $3$ respectively. This curve can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(x+y)\\,i+(1-x)\\,j \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-6({sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-6)\\,dt \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-6t]_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[1+0-6\\pi ]-[-1+3-3\\pi ] \\\\  & =-1-3\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535202 true] [17592186337302 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337303 13194139535202 true] [17592186337302 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337304 13194139535202 true] [17592186337302 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337305 13194139535202 true] [17592186337302 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337306 13194139535202 true] [17592186337302 1000 #edb/ref 17592186337307 131